  "id": "COMPOUND:798 - PROTEIN:861",
  "verbalization": "Sodium lauryl sulfate is implicated in the pathway leading to Retinoic acid receptor alpha through multiple indirect routes. The first pathway connects Sodium lauryl sulfate to T-24, which in turn targets Retinoic acid receptor alpha. The second and third pathways link Sodium lauryl sulfate to Potassium-transporting ATPase subunit beta, which targets 13-cis-Retinol, and subsequently to Retinoic acid receptor alpha. These findings suggest that Sodium lauryl sulfate may influence Retinoic acid receptor alpha through a series of molecular interactions involving lipid metabolism and retinoid signaling. The evidence supports a potential role for Sodium lauryl sulfate in modulating retinoic acid receptor alpha activity, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights the complex interplay between lipid-based compounds and retinoic acid receptor signaling, emphasizing the need for further investigation into the molecular mechanisms underlying this relationship.",
